Hi and welcome.

First of all, since your new to the list you probably have missed the
recent "requests" for 5.0 & 6.0 support in the package.  FYI, these
chip types are roughly supported in the sense that they can be loaded
and analysis (an optimal model is different story), but I still have
to fine tune the details, especially on annotation files.  I'll have
to ask you to bear with me on this one, because I would take me too
long to go through and explain the details.  I'll post an example when
it is all there.

If you want to get going with a full analysis, while I'm preparing for
6.0, I recommend you to download 5-10 500K samples and play with that.
 My aim is that the 5.0 & 6.0 scripts will look the same.

